WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.430
- Whats weirdest thing

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:03.360
you found yourself doing in quarantine?

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:06.140
Cause I have found myself
doing some incredibly odd

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:07.290
things that I never would have done.

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:08.250
But there's just you know,

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:09.980
sometimes you're forced into it.

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:10.813
- Let me tell you.

00:00:10.813 --> 00:00:11.894
I mean yeah the time

00:00:11.894 --> 00:00:15.070
is weird when you're in quarantine.

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:17.090
Luckily I'm writing a memoir

00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:19.560
so that's really occupied
a good portion of my time,

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.920
which has been fun to
go back over your life

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:25.370
I wish everybody can do this.

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:26.920
Not that you would have to publish it

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:28.360
- I've never told anybody this

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:30.990
I'm literally been writing
mine like separately

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:31.900
because I was like,

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:33.300
this is such a crazy story.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.340
You're totally right.

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:37.350
You kind of get to go
back through your life.

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:38.520
Isn't that the best,

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.280
cause you get to live again,

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:41.113
it's the best.

00:00:41.113 --> 00:00:42.200
And then you're also like,

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.630
you just hopefully you're wiser,

00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:45.850
you know now and you look back

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:46.683
and you're like God,

00:00:46.683 --> 00:00:47.650
that seam

00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:48.483
- I know

00:00:48.483 --> 00:00:49.440
- It's no different then,

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.140
- And like getting outside the bubble that

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:52.620
- Oh my God

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:54.060
- The idea that I used to,

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:55.430
there was one time I
was thinking of writing

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:59.570
this story of the day where
I was hitchhiking to kiss

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:01.930
and it was like

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:04.030
You know I had no idea how
I was going to get there.

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:06.260
I had no idea how I was going to get home,

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:09.230
but I had tickets to kiss

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:10.407
and I had this

00:01:10.407 --> 00:01:11.240
- (laughing)

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:13.560
and I had to get there. I don't know how.

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:16.220
So I just hitchhiked to put my thumb out

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:18.480
and then some random guy

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:20.657
- Dateline special but okay (laughing).

00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:24.160
- You know i had the platform shoes on.

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:26.030
I was ready to rock.

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:28.454
- Oh my God I mean you do.

00:01:28.454 --> 00:01:29.330
That's the thing.

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:31.230
When you find yourself
writing about your life,

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:33.320
like even me moving out
to LA I had no idea.

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:34.153
No job.

00:01:34.153 --> 00:01:35.200
I had nowhere to live.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:36.210
but I just went.

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:37.872
I was just like it's just the same.

00:01:37.872 --> 00:01:38.705
- You know

00:01:38.705 --> 00:01:39.538
- You just have to do it.

00:01:39.538 --> 00:01:42.223
- There's something to
being young and dumb,

00:01:42.223 --> 00:01:43.160
- 100%

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:44.200
- Right?

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.140
Because if you thought
about it I'd be like,

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:47.630
what you did what?

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:49.635
- I would never let my children.

00:01:49.635 --> 00:01:50.750
- (laughing) Never

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:53.325
- Well I'm like no you're
not allowed to do that.

00:01:53.325 --> 00:01:54.473
- Oh my God

